# Expectation record for 09_optimization_levels/007_struct_copy_invariance.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 007_struct_copy_invariance
area               = 09_optimization_levels
description        = Aggregate construction, copy, return and pass by value across optimization levels
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Every member of every aggregate is assigned before it is read, so no indeterminate value
and no padding byte is ever observed; aggregates are compared member by member rather than
by their object representation.  All member values stay inside the range of their types.
Which shapes travel in registers and which in memory is the ABI's decision, and only the
retrieved member values are compared.  Every property is computed twice, once from literal constants and once from
volatile-qualified storage, so the constant folder's answer cannot stand in for the
one the backend computes at run time.
No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
small a=5 b=10
small_copy a=5 b=10
small_byvalue=15
boundary a=5 b=6 c=7 d=8
boundary_copy a=5 b=6 c=7 d=8
boundary_byvalue=26
mixed tag=5 value=6.750
mixed_copy tag=5 value=6.750
large v[0]=5 copy_v[0]=5
large v[1]=8 copy_v[1]=8
large v[2]=11 copy_v[2]=11
large v[3]=14 copy_v[3]=14
large v[4]=17 copy_v[4]=17
large v[5]=20 copy_v[5]=20
large v[6]=23 copy_v[6]=23
large v[7]=26 copy_v[7]=26
large checksum=124 flag=1
large_copy checksum=124 flag=1
large_byvalue=249
END
